  "notes": {
    "arrival": "Load holds near 222 a minute with short spikes. Within a second it peaks at 13 requests, which is the burst a Poisson generator at the same average almost never makes.",
    "prompts": "Half the prompts are under 11.6K tokens, and one in ten is over 38.6K. The long tail is where prefill time and KV size grow fastest.",
    "turns": "A turn joins a session when its leading block hashes match an earlier request for at least two blocks, using the longest match. 1,672 requests continue an earlier one, and that chain accounts for 100% of all reused blocks.",
    "gaps": "The median follow-up lands 64 seconds later and one in ten waits over 5 minutes. A cache has to hold that context the whole time or the next turn pays full prefill again.",
    "kv": "This trace needs about 5.4 TiB of KV on a dense GQA model and 0.2 TiB on a hybrid model with few attention layers. That gap decides whether host memory is enough or a shared tier is needed."
  },
